oolu_011d5qFzMReYuPqWrq5e9qpg","tool_input":{"command":"git status --short; npm ls typescript 2>&1 | head -5; git diff 8267db3..HEAD -- npm-shrinkwrap.json | grep -nE '^[-+] *\"(typescript|@types/node)\"'; grep -n lockfileVersion npm-shrinkwrap.json; ls node_modules/@typescript 2>&1 | head -3"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QRDhJ2JnJwzsufdMfKd7PD","tool_input":{"command":"npx tsc --version"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":15,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Approving PKT-0009. I did not rerun the acceptance commands, as instructed, and `npx tsc` needed approval so I didn't run it. I read the diff and the shrinkwrap instead.\n\n- **Scope:** every changed file is in `target.files`, or is a new root file (`tsconfig.json`, `ts-strip.js`) allowed by `create_in: [.]`. `Makefile`, `commondefines.js` and `license.js` are untouched. The change touches 11 files against a budget of 14, well under the line limit. `tests/jest.config.js` and the unit tests are unchanged.\n- **Previous rejections are fixed:**\n  - The generated `utilsDocService.js` is no longer tracked. `git ls-files` shows only the `.ts`, and the `.gitignore` and `.prettierignore` entries now take effect.\n  - `typescript@^7.0.2` and `@types/node` are root devDependencies. The shrinkwrap stays at `lockfileVersion: 1` and carries the real `typescript` entry, with its `requires` list and per-platform packages including `linux-x64`.\n- **No stale `.js` can satisfy the oracle:** `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` runs `node ts-strip.js` before Jest, and the root test scripts do the same. The Dockerfile runs `npm run build:ts` before `pkg`, which doesn't need dev dependencies because Node erases the types.\n- **Behavior is preserved:**\n  - The `module.exports` names are identical, still plain CommonJS.\n  - The `localeToLCID` rewrite (`lang ? locale[lang.toLowerCase()] : undefined`) returns the same results as the old `locale[lang && lang.toLowerCase()]` for `''`, `null` and `undefined`.\n  - `decodeHeicToSharp` now takes the loaded sharp module as a parameter, but it isn't exported and gets the same instance as before.\n  - The `(e as Error).stack` and `.message` casts keep the old behavior.\n- **Type-stripping is safe:** `tsconfig.json` sets `erasableSyntaxOnly`, so non-erasable syntax is caught by `tsc` before the build step, which would throw on it.\n- **Interop doc:** it records the output-location decision (`.js` next to the `.ts`), the Jest strategy, the options checked against TS 7, a migration checklist and the pitfalls.\n\n**Gaps that don't block approval:**\n- The `.ts` lint follow-up packet is still not created, and \"Spawned packets\" is empty. The doc explains why: the factory run forbade writes under `.theseus/queue/`. Someone with queue access needs to run `theseus packet new` for it, since I can't change files.\n- `prepare: node ts-strip.js` runs on every root `npm install`. That's harmless, and it needs Node 22.13 or newer, which the image provides.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Scope and contract respected; generated .js untracked, real v1 shrinkwrap with typescript 7.0.2, oracle rebuilds before Jest, exports and behavior unchanged. The .ts lint follow-up packet still has to be created by someone with queue access.","ttft_ms":2619,"type":"result","duration_ms":38928,"uuid":"b7a724a3-f070-45a1-8b37-dc72b0c68d0b","ttft_stream_ms":1454,"time_to_request_ms":445,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":195,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":25,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":58